  "result": "Fixed. Subcommands now read their own entry from a nested `default_map`, so `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` sets `runserver`'s `--port` to 5000.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py`, a subcommand's `Context` inherited the parent's whole `default_map` (`default_map = parent.default_map`). Its parameter lookups then ran against the top-level dict, so the `\"runserver\"` entry was never used. The docs describe the map as nested per subcommand, so the code was wrong.\n\n**Change:** `src/click/core.py:392` now reads `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_nested_for_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It checks that one subcommand gets its nested default and another subcommand with no entry keeps its own parameter default. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n**Results:** The full suite passes: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. Say if you want one.",
